---
import MarketingLayout from "../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro";
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Security · Gatewerk"
  description="Plain facts about how Gatewerk handles your data and your decisions. No badges. The source is open; every claim can be checked against it."
>

  <!-- ─── ambient glow ─── -->
  <div style="position:absolute;top:-260px;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);width:1100px;height:600px;background:radial-gradient(ellipse at center,rgba(33,181,113,.1),transparent 68%);pointer-events:none;filter:blur(20px);z-index:0;"></div>

  <section style="position:relative;z-index:1;max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;padding:84px 32px 96px;">

    <h1 class="gw-up gw-display" style="font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(34px,5vw,48px);line-height:1.06;letter-spacing:-.03em;color:#f7f7f1;margin:0;">Security</h1>
    <p class="gw-up" style="max-width:640px;margin:22px 0 0;font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:#b4b4ac;text-wrap:pretty;">
      Plain facts about how Gatewerk handles your data and your decisions. No
      badges. The source is open; every claim on this page can be checked
      against it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="gw-display" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,28px);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:#f7f7f1;margin:56px 0 0;">Self hosted by default</h2>
    <p style="margin:20px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#9a9a8f;">
      Gatewerk is open source and runs on your infrastructure. Your reviews,
      payloads, and decision history live in your Postgres database on your
      server. The self hosted build sends nothing to us.
    </p>

    <h2 class="gw-display" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,28px);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:#f7f7f1;margin:56px 0 0;">The audit record</h2>
    <p style="margin:20px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#9a9a8f;">
      Every action is written to an append only audit log. Entries are HMAC
      signed and chained: each entry's signature covers its predecessor, so
      deleting or rewriting history breaks the chain and verification fails.
      The record preserves every distinction of the process: approved,
      rejected, edited, vetoed, or confirmed, attributed to the specific human
      or explicitly to the system.
    </p>
    <p style="margin:16px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#9a9a8f;">
      The record is tamper evident, not tamper proof. An operator who holds
      both the signing secret and database write access could rebuild a chain.
      Keep the signing secret out of the hands that hold the database.
    </p>

    <h2 class="gw-display" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,28px);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:#f7f7f1;margin:56px 0 0;">Webhooks</h2>
    <p style="margin:20px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#9a9a8f;">
      Every delivery is signed with HMAC-SHA256, in three envelopes: a simple
      v1 signature for authenticity, a v2 envelope with a timestamp for replay
      protection, and Standard Webhooks compatible signatures for receivers
      that already speak that spec. Deliveries carry a stable idempotency key
      so receivers can deduplicate retries.
    </p>

    <h2 class="gw-display" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,28px);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:#f7f7f1;margin:56px 0 0;">Callback URL protection</h2>
    <p style="margin:20px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#9a9a8f;">
      Callback URLs are validated against SSRF: private and link local address
      ranges are refused, with DNS resolution checked, so a review request
      cannot be used to probe your internal network.
    </p>

    <h2 class="gw-display" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,28px);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:#f7f7f1;margin:56px 0 0;">Authentication</h2>
    <p style="margin:20px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#9a9a8f;">
      API keys are scoped, stored as SHA-256 hashes, and shown once at
      creation. Rotation is built in. Dashboard sessions are separate from
      agent credentials, and management endpoints require session
      authentication, not an API key.
    </p>

    <h2 class="gw-display" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,28px);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:#f7f7f1;margin:56px 0 0;">Reporting a vulnerability</h2>
    <p style="margin:20px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#9a9a8f;">
      Email <a href="mailto:security@gatewerk.com" style="color:#e4e0d6;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;">security@gatewerk.com</a>. We will acknowledge within 72 hours. Please
      do not open a public issue for a vulnerability before we have had a
      chance to fix it.
    </p>

    <div style="margin-top:56px;border-top:1px solid rgba(240,240,220,.08);padding-top:32px;">
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:#8f887c;">
        This page is dated and kept current. Public since 2026-08-14.
      </p>
    </div>

  </section>

</MarketingLayout>
